{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he lifted up the staff and struck the waters</b> — that he raised and stretched out his hand over the land of Egypt against all directions of the wind, and after that he struck the waters that were in the river before Pharaoh's eyes, and all the waters that were in the river turned to blood before his eyes, and the blood was yet throughout all the land of Egypt. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 7:20) that Scripture mentioned the plague of the river but did not bother to mention the stretching out of his hand over all the land of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:39.352808815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}